{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-right: 33.1pt;&quot;&gt;The proposal, by\r\nreason of its preponderance of smaller 1-bed units, would result in an\r\ninappropriate and inadequate housing mix, having regard to the location of the\r\nsite and the character of its surroundings as well as the evidence of local\r\nneed which identifies the need for more larger family sized units, and would\r\nfail to create inclusive and mixed communities to the detriment of the\r\nstrategic objectives of the Harrow Core Policy CS1.A and CS1.I, and Policy\r\nH10.A of The London Plan (2021) and policy DM24 of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan (2013).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;paragraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-top: 5pt; margin-right: 33.1pt; margin-bottom: 5pt;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposal, by reason of its massing and design, would result in a development\r\nwhich would be excessive in scale, excessively bulky, visually obtrusive and\r\nunduly prominent when viewed in the street scene, and which would fail to be in\r\nkeeping with the prevailing pattern of buildings within the area and within its\r\nlocal context. The proposal would thereby be contrary to the high quality\r\ndesign aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies\r\nD3.D(1) and D3.D(11) of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B of the Harrow\r\nCore Strategy (2012), Policies DM1.A and DM1.B of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Policies Local Plan (2013), and the adopted Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
